{
  "rationale": "This is iteration 0, so there is no race telemetry or integration feedback yet. The geometry is a conservative baseline built from the contract's physics and sensing rules.\n\nSensing: 12 mm sensor footprints are smaller than the 25 mm tape, so one footprint can sit fully on the tape while the others read background. Five sensors at 20 mm pitch span 80 mm, which covers the tape at the centre and in moderate offsets. Placing them 50 mm ahead of the axle gives the controller a lookahead on bends, so steering starts before the wheels reach the curve. Symmetric placement avoids a built-in left or right bias.\n\nBody: wheel_track 0.12 m and wheel_radius 0.03 m are mid-range values that give a stable turn rate and enough torque margin for a 1.5 m/s average. Body_width 0.12 m keeps the off-track limit at its 0.06 m floor, since tape_half_width + body_width/4 = 0.0425 m is below it. Widening the body further does not change the limit until body_width exceeds about 0.19 m, so there is no benefit from going wider. Mass 0.8 kg and body_length 0.16 m keep yaw inertia moderate, which limits oscillation on the slalom.\n\nExpected result: a complete run on the oval and s-bend with few line-loss events. The slalom is the main risk, because the lateral sensor spread may not hold the line through quick direction changes. The race data should show whether that holds.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": 0.04, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.04, "y": 0.05}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "intent": "Baseline geometry: five 12 mm sensors spread 80 mm across the line and 50 mm ahead of the axle, for lookahead. Moderate track, wheel and mass values. Purpose: get a clean first race and measure how well this layout holds the line on the slalom and on tight bends. Next iteration, adjust sensor spread and forward offset from the Integrator's feedback and the race telemetry.",
  "feedback_request": {
    "measurements": ["completion", "progress", "completion_time", "rms_error", "max_error", "line_loss_events", "steering_oscillation", "control_effort", "controller_errors", "noise_robustness"]
  },
  "learning": "No evidence yet. Hypotheses to test: (1) forward sensor offset of 50 mm improves tight-bend tracking versus a sensor line at the axle; (2) 80 mm sensor spread keeps at least one sensor on the tape at the slalom's largest lateral offset; (3) a 0.8 kg mass with 0.12 m track gives enough turn authority for the sharpest bends without slip."
}
